WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.896
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:06.196 --> 00:00:09.547
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.847 --> 00:00:16.726
Unit ten: Paraphrasing and Summarising. Today you will restate ideas in your own words without copying.

4
00:00:17.026 --> 00:00:19.562
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.826
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:25.824
Paraphrase.

7
00:00:26.817 --> 00:00:29.490
Paraphrase means to say again in different words.

8
00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:31.723
Paraphrase the sentence.

9
00:00:32.317 --> 00:00:35.282
Your turn. Say: Paraphrase.

10
00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:39.332
Paraphrase.

11
00:00:40.083 --> 00:00:41.038
Summary.

12
00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.676
Summary means a short version of main points.

13
00:00:45.283 --> 00:00:46.447
Write a summary.

14
00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.842
Your turn. Say: Summary.

15
00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:53.539
Summary.

16
00:00:54.283 --> 00:00:55.133
Synonym.

17
00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:58.451
Synonym means a word with the same meaning.

18
00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:00.283
Use a synonym.

19
00:01:00.883 --> 00:01:03.327
Your turn. Say: Synonym.

20
00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:07.052
Synonym.

21
00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:08.795
Original.

22
00:01:09.783 --> 00:01:11.609
Original means from the source.

23
00:01:12.217 --> 00:01:13.705
Keep the original meaning.

24
00:01:14.317 --> 00:01:16.957
Your turn. Say: Original.

25
00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:20.755
Original.

26
00:01:21.517 --> 00:01:22.448
Structure.

27
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.647
Structure means the way a sentence is built.

28
00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.052
Change the sentence structure.

29
00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:31.186
Your turn. Say: Structure.

30
00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:35.139
Structure.

31
00:01:35.883 --> 00:01:36.942
Condense.

32
00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.822
Condense means to make shorter.

33
00:01:40.417 --> 00:01:41.789
Condense the text.

34
00:01:42.383 --> 00:01:44.571
Your turn. Say: Condense.

35
00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:48.516
Condense.

36
00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.135
Accurate.

37
00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:53.637
Accurate means correct in every detail.

38
00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:55.507
Keep it accurate.

39
00:01:56.117 --> 00:01:58.258
Your turn. Say: Accurate.

40
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.171
Accurate.

41
00:02:02.917 --> 00:02:03.941
Essential.

42
00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.984
Essential means very important.

43
00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:10.059
Include only essential points.

44
00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:13.778
Your turn. Say: Essential.

45
00:02:16.633 --> 00:02:17.588
Essential.

46
00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.260
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.117 --> 00:02:25.836
Visal, how do I paraphrase a sentence?

48
00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:38.020
Read it, close the book and write the idea from memory in your own words. Change the vocabulary with synonyms and change the sentence structure, but keep the meaning.

49
00:02:39.117 --> 00:02:40.989
What is the difference from a summary?

50
00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:50.843
A paraphrase has about the same length as the original. A summary is much shorter and includes only the essential points.

51
00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:53.276
What should I avoid?

52
00:02:54.383 --> 00:03:03.610
Avoid copying phrases and changing only one or two words. Do not add your own opinion. Always name the source of the idea.

53
00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:06.093
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:11.132
Grammar focus: Changing structure: active and passive.

55
00:03:11.432 --> 00:03:12.712
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:13.417 --> 00:03:15.428
Scientists published the report.

57
00:03:16.317 --> 00:03:18.781
The report was published by scientists.

58
00:03:19.733 --> 00:03:26.714
Change the structure to paraphrase: the active sentence Scientists published the report becomes The report was published by scientists.

59
00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:31.066
Be careful! Don't say: I copy but change one word.

60
00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.917
Say: I rewrite the idea in my own words.

61
00:03:36.217 --> 00:03:37.462
Do not copy.

62
00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:40.884
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.119
In My Own Words.

64
00:03:43.419 --> 00:03:46.220
Sokha reads a paragraph about renewable energy.

65
00:03:47.233 --> 00:03:50.347
She closes the book and writes the main idea from memory.

66
00:03:51.333 --> 00:03:54.656
She uses synonyms and changes the sentence structure.

67
00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:58.096
She checks that the meaning is still accurate.

68
00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.320
Finally she adds the name of the source.

69
00:04:02.433 --> 00:04:06.911
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:10.516
To paraphrase is to say it in blank words.

71
00:04:10.816 --> 00:04:13.889
A, no. B, different. C, the same.

72
00:04:17.433 --> 00:04:19.317
The answer is B: different.

73
00:04:20.483 --> 00:04:22.576
A summary is blank than the original.

74
00:04:22.876 --> 00:04:26.355
A, longer. B, louder. C, shorter.

75
00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:31.876
The answer is C: shorter.

76
00:04:33.017 --> 00:04:34.877
A synonym has the same blank.

77
00:04:35.177 --> 00:04:38.587
A, meaning. B, sound. C, colour.

78
00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:43.610
The answer is A: meaning.

79
00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.668
You must keep the blank accurate.

80
00:04:46.968 --> 00:04:50.761
A, title. B, meaning. C, spelling only.

81
00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.218
The answer is B: meaning.

82
00:04:57.383 --> 00:04:59.244
What does Sokha add at the end?

83
00:04:59.544 --> 00:05:03.418
A, a joke. B, a picture. C, the source.

84
00:05:06.967 --> 00:05:09.245
The answer is C: the source.

85
00:05:10.433 --> 00:05:13.457
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:14.317 --> 00:05:15.829
How do you paraphrase?

87
00:05:24.617 --> 00:05:26.233
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:26.533 --> 00:05:39.567
I read the sentence, close the book and write the idea from memory. I use synonyms and change the sentence structure but keep the meaning accurate. Then I name the source.

89
00:05:39.867 --> 00:05:41.565
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:48.272
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and changing structure: active and passive.

91
00:05:48.572 --> 00:05:54.220
Today's value is intellectual honesty. Follow the evidence, even when it is inconvenient.

92
00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.893
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

93
00:05:57.193 --> 00:06:00.240
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

